[[sn:Nine Stars]] [[ja:九星]] [[en:Nine Stars]] [[ar:Nine Stars]]

{{distinguish|3=Navagraha|qq=}}
{{Cite source|date=December 2018|qq=}}
{{color|qq=}} '''Nine Stars''' ({{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|qq=}}, Kyūsei) is a form of [[folk belief]] originating from ancient [[China]], consisting of nine stars: '''First White''', '''Second Black''', '''Third Blue''', '''Fourth Green''', '''Fifth Yellow''', '''Sixth White''', '''Seventh Red''', '''Eighth White''', and '''Ninth Purple'''.
The term "Nine Stars" can refer to several systems, and the one described here is specifically referred to as the "Purple White Nine Stars" or "Seven Colored Stars."
== Origin == The Nine Stars system originates from the following {{ill|magic square|ja|魔方陣|qq=}}:
== Nine Stars Comparison Chart == {{main|{{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|qq=}}|qq=}} {| class="wikitable" |- ! style="background:green;color:white;" |{{ill|Fourth Green Wood Star|ja|四緑木星|lt=4🌳|qq=}} !! style="background:purple;color:white;" |{{ill|Ninth Purple Fire Star|ja|九紫火星|lt=9🔥|qq=}} !! style="background:black;color:white;" |{{ill|Second Black Earth Star|ja|二黒土星|lt=2🪨|qq=}} |- ! style="background:blue;color:white;" |{{ill|Third Blue Wood Star|ja|三碧木星|lt=3🌳|qq=}} !! style="background:yellow;" |{{ill|Fifth Yellow Earth Star|ja|五黄土星|lt=5🪨|qq=}} !! style="background:red;color:white;" |{{ill|Seventh Red Metal Star|ja|七赤金星|lt=7🪙|qq=}} |- !style="background:white;"|{{ill|Eighth White Earth Star|ja|八白土星|lt=8🪨|qq=}} !style="background:white;"|{{ill|First White Water Star|ja|一白水星|lt=1💧|qq=}} !style="background:white;"|{{ill|Sixth White Metal Star|ja|六白金星|lt=6🪙|qq=}} |}
In this magic square, the sum of any row, column, or diagonal equals 15. It uses the numbers 1 through 9 exactly once in a 3×3 grid. This configuration, called the '''Later Heaven Arrangement''' ({{ill|Later Heaven Arrangement|ja|後天定位盤|qq=}}), is the only one of its kind, excluding rotations and reflections. These numbers are paired with seven colors (white, black, blue, green, yellow, red, and purple), the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=}} ({{ill|wood|ja|木|qq=}}, {{ill|fire|ja|火|qq=}}, {{ill|earth|ja|土|qq=}}, {{ill|metal (wuxing)|ja|金|lt=metal|qq=}}, and {{ill|water|ja|水|qq=}}), the {{ill|ten heavenly stems|ja|十干|qq=}}, the {{ill|twelve earthly branches|ja|十二支|qq=}}, and the {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=}} of {{ill|I Ching|ja|易経|qq=}}. When these numbers shift positions, interpretations are added to form the "Nine Stars."
According to legend, {{ill|Yu the Great|ja|禹|qq=}}, founder of the {{ill|Xia Dynasty|ja|夏王朝|1=Xia dynasty|qq=}}, conceived this magic square when he encountered a sacred turtle emerging from the {{ill|Luo River|ja|洛水|qq=}}. This magic square is called the "Writing of the Luo" ({{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|洛書|qq=}}), one of the {{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|河図洛書|qq=}}.
== The Nine Stars == In Japanese {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=}}, the following table associates the Nine Stars with the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=}}, {{ill|directions|ja|方位|qq=}}, {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=}}, and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|qq=}} of directions based on a person's birth year.
== Nine Stars Comparison Chart == {| class="wikitable" |- ! Star ! Reading ! Five Element ! Direction ! Eight Trigram ! Color |- ! {{ill|First White Water Star|ja|一白水星|1=First White Water Star|qq=}} | Ippaku Suisei | Water | {{ill|North|ja|北|qq=}} | {{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|qq=}} | style="background:white;"| White |- ! {{ill|Second Black Earth Star|ja|二黒土星|1=Second Black Earth Star|qq=}} | Jikoku Dosei | Earth | Southwest | {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|qq=}} | style="background:black;color:white;"| Black |- ! {{ill|Third Blue Wood Star|ja|三碧木星|1=Third Blue Wood Star|qq=}} | Sanpeki Mokusei | Wood | {{ill|East|ja|東|qq=}} | {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|qq=}} | style="background:blue;color:white;"| Blue |- ! {{ill|Fourth Green Wood Star|ja|四緑木星|1=Fourth Green Wood Star|qq=}} | Shiroku Mokusei | Wood | Southeast | {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|qq=}} | style="background:green;color:white;"| Green |- ! {{ill|Fifth Yellow Earth Star|1=Fifth Yellow Earth Star|ja|五黄土星|qq=}} | Goō Dosei | Earth | Center | {{ill|Taiji (philosophy)|ja|太極|fr|Taiji (philosophie)|ru|Великий предел|ja|太極|lt=Taiji|qq=}} | style="background:yellow;"| Yellow |- ! {{ill|Sixth White Metal Star|1=Sixth White Metal Star|ja|六白金星|qq=}} | Roppaku Kinsei | Metal | Northwest | {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|qq=}} | style="background:white;"| White |- ! {{ill|Seventh Red Metal Star|1=Seventh Red Metal Star|ja|七赤金星|qq=}} | Shichiseki Kinsei | Metal | {{ill|West|ja|西|qq=}} | {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|qq=}} | style="background:red;color:white;"| Red |- ! {{ill|Eighth White Earth Star|1=Eighth White Earth Star|ja|八白土星|qq=}} | Happaku Dosei | Earth | Northeast | {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|qq=}} | style="background:white;"| White |- ! {{ill|Ninth Purple Fire Star|1=Ninth Purple Fire Star|ja|九紫火星|qq=}} | Kyūshi Kasei | Fire | {{ill|South|ja|南|qq=}} | {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|qq=}} | style="background:purple;color:white;"| Purple |}
Despite their names, the Nine Stars are not related to celestial objects like the planets in the {{ill|Solar System|ja|太陽系|qq=}}.
== Relationships Among the Stars == The relationships among the Nine Stars follow the {{ill|five elements theory|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=}}:
== Nine Stars Comparison Chart == {| class="wikitable" |- ! Star ! Beneficial (Compatible) ! Neutral (Compatible) ! Harmful (Incompatible) |- ! First White Water Star | Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star, Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star | First White Water Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star |- ! Second Black Earth Star | Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | First White Water Star, Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star |- ! Third Blue Wood Star | First White Water Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star | Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star, Eighth White Earth Star |- ! Fourth Green Wood Star | First White Water Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star | Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star, Eighth White Earth Star |- ! Fifth Yellow Earth Star | Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | First White Water Star, Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star |- ! Sixth White Metal Star | First White Water Star, Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star | Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star |- ! Seventh Red Metal Star | First White Water Star, Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star | Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star |- ! Eighth White Earth Star | Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star, Ninth Purple Fire Star | Second Black Earth Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | First White Water Star, Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star |- ! Ninth Purple Fire Star | Second Black Earth Star, Third Blue Wood Star, Fourth Green Wood Star, Fifth Yellow Earth Star, Eighth White Earth Star | Ninth Purple Fire Star | First White Water Star, Sixth White Metal Star, Seventh Red Metal Star |}
These relationships are used for predicting {{ill|astrological compatibility|lt=compatibility|ja|相性|nl|Synastrie|ru|Синастрическая астрология|sq|Sinastria|ja|相性|en|qq=}}, {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=}}, and {{ill|auspicious directions|ja|吉方位|qq=}}.
