== The Nine Stars == In Japanese {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=|12=draft}}, the following table associates the Nine Stars with the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|directions|ja|方位|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=|12=draft}}, and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=|12=draft}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|qq=|12=draft}} of directions based on a person's birth year.
