{{Cite source|date=December 2018|qq=}}
{{color|qq=}} '''Nine Stars''' ({{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nine Stars|qq=}}, Kyūsei) is a form of [[folk belief]] originating from ancient [[China]], consisting of nine stars: '''First White''', '''Second Black''', '''Third Blue''', '''Fourth Green''', '''Fifth Yellow''', '''Sixth White''', '''Seventh Red''', '''Eighth White''', and '''Ninth Purple'''.
The term "Nine Stars" can refer to several systems, and the one described here is specifically referred to as the "Purple White Nine Stars" or "Seven Colored Stars."
== Origin == The Nine Stars system originates from the following {{ill|magic square|ja|魔方陣|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/magic square|qq=}}:
== Nine Stars Comparison Chart == {{main|{{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nine Stars|qq=}}|qq=}} {| class="wikitable" |- ! style="background:green;color:white;" |{{ill|Fourth Green Wood Star|ja|四緑木星|lt=4🌳|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fourth Green Wood Star|qq=}} !! style="background:purple;color:white;" |{{ill|Ninth Purple Fire Star|ja|九紫火星|lt=9🔥|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ninth Purple Fire Star|qq=}} !! style="background:black;color:white;" |{{ill|Second Black Earth Star|ja|二黒土星|lt=2🪨|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Second Black Earth Star|qq=}} |- ! style="background:blue;color:white;" |{{ill|Third Blue Wood Star|ja|三碧木星|lt=3🌳|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Third Blue Wood Star|qq=}} !! style="background:yellow;" |{{ill|Fifth Yellow Earth Star|ja|五黄土星|lt=5🪨|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fifth Yellow Earth Star|qq=}} !! style="background:red;color:white;" |{{ill|Seventh Red Metal Star|ja|七赤金星|lt=7🪙|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Seventh Red Metal Star|qq=}} |- !style="background:white;"|{{ill|Eighth White Earth Star|ja|八白土星|lt=8🪨|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Eighth White Earth Star|qq=}} !style="background:white;"|{{ill|First White Water Star|ja|一白水星|lt=1💧|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/First White Water Star|qq=}} !style="background:white;"|{{ill|Sixth White Metal Star|ja|六白金星|lt=6🪙|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sixth White Metal Star|qq=}} |}
In this magic square, the sum of any row, column, or diagonal equals 15. It uses the numbers 1 through 9 exactly once in a 3×3 grid. This configuration, called the '''Later Heaven Arrangement''' ({{ill|Later Heaven Arrangement|ja|後天定位盤|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Later Heaven Arrangement|qq=}}), is the only one of its kind, excluding rotations and reflections. These numbers are paired with seven colors (white, black, blue, green, yellow, red, and purple), the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|qq=}} ({{ill|wood|ja|木|1=Wood (wuxing)|lt=Wood (木)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/wood|qq=}}, {{ill|fire|ja|火|1=Fire (wuxing)|lt=Fire (火)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fire|qq=}}, {{ill|earth|ja|土|1=Earth (wuxing)|lt=Earth (土)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/earth|qq=}}, {{ill|metal (wuxing)|ja|金|1=Metal (wuxing)|lt=Metal (金)|lt=metal|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/metal (wuxing)|qq=}}, and {{ill|water|zh|水|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|lt=Water (水)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/water|qq=}}), the {{ill|ten heavenly stems|ja|十干|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/ten heavenly stems|qq=}}, the {{ill|twelve earthly branches|ja|十二支|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/twelve earthly branches|qq=}}, and the {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/eight trigrams|qq=}} of {{ill|I Ching|ja|易経|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/I Ching|qq=}}. When these numbers shift positions, interpretations are added to form the "Nine Stars."
According to legend, {{ill|Yu the Great|ja|禹|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yu the Great|qq=}}, founder of the {{ill|Xia Dynasty|ja|夏王朝|1=Xia dynasty|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|qq=}}, conceived this magic square when he encountered a sacred turtle emerging from the {{ill|Luo River|ja|洛水|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|qq=}}. This magic square is called the "Writing of the Luo" ({{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}), one of the {{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|河図洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}.
== The Nine Stars == In Japanese {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōdō|qq=}}, the following table associates the Nine Stars with the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|qq=}}, {{ill|directions|ja|方位|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/directions|qq=}}, {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/eight trigrams|qq=}}, and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|qq=}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|qq=}} of directions based on a person's birth year.
