In this magic square, the sum of any row, column, or diagonal equals 15. It uses the numbers 1 through 9 exactly once in a 3×3 grid. This configuration, called the '''Later Heaven Arrangement''' ({{ill|Later Heaven Arrangement|ja|後天定位盤|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Later Heaven Arrangement|qq=}}), is the only one of its kind, excluding rotations and reflections. These numbers are paired with seven colors (white, black, blue, green, yellow, red, and purple), the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|qq=}} ({{ill|wood|ja|Wood (木)|1=Wood (wuxing)|lt=Wood (木)|2=uk|3=Дерево (елемент)|4=id|5=Kayu (Wu Xing)|6=ms|7=Kayu (Wu Xing)|8=bcl|9=Kahoy (wuxing)|10=ca|11=Fusta (wuxing)|12=it|13=Legno (elemento)|14=es|15=Madera (Wu Xing)|16=nl|17=Hout (element)|18=vi|19=Mộc (Ngũ hành)|20=tr|21=Tahta (klasik element)|22=ta|23=மரம் (சீன மெய்யியல்)|2=it|3=Legno (elemento)|4=es|5=Madera (Wu Xing)|6=tr|7=Tahta (klasik element)|1=Wood (wuxing)|lt=Wood (木)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/wood|qq=}}, {{ill|fire|ja|火|1=Fire (wuxing)|lt=Fire (火)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fire|qq=}}, {{ill|earth|ja|Earth (土)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Earth (wuxing)|lt=Earth (土)|2=ru|3=Земля (у-син)|4=mn|5=Шороо (махбод)|6=uk|7=Земля (У-сін)|8=als|9=Ärde in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|10=bcl|11=Daga (wuxing)|12=vi|13=Thổ (Ngũ hành)|1=Earth (wuxing)|lt=Earth (土)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/earth|qq=}}, {{ill|Metal (wuxing)|ja|金|lt=Metal (金)|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/metal (wuxing)}}, and {{ill|water|zh|Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|lt=Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/water|qq=}}), the {{ill|ten heavenly stems|ja|十干|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/ten heavenly stems|qq=}}, the {{ill|twelve earthly branches|ja|十二支|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/twelve earthly branches|qq=}}, and the {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/eight trigrams|qq=}} of {{ill|I Ching|ja|易経|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/I Ching|qq=}}. When these numbers shift positions, interpretations are added to form the "Nine Stars."

According to legend, {{ill|Yu the Great|ja|禹|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yu the Great|qq=}}, founder of the {{ill|Xia Dynasty|ja|夏王朝|1=Xia dynasty|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|qq=}}, conceived this magic square when he encountered a sacred turtle emerging from the {{ill|Luo River|ja|洛水|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|qq=}}. This magic square is called the "Writing of the Luo" ({{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}), one of the {{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|河図洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}.

== The Nine Stars ==
In Japanese {{ill|Onmyōdō|ja|陰陽道|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onmyōdō|qq=}}, the following table associates the Nine Stars with the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=five elements|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|qq=}}, {{ill|directions|ja|方位|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/directions|qq=}}, {{ill|eight trigrams|ja|八卦|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/eight trigrams|qq=}}, and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|qq=}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|qq=}} of directions based on a person's birth year.

