'''Nine Stars''' ({{ill|Nine Stars|ja|九星|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nine Stars|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nine Stars|qq=}}, Kyūsei) is a form of [[folk belief]] originating from ancient [[China]], consisting of nine stars: '''First White''', '''Second Black''', '''Third Blue''', '''Fourth Green''', '''Fifth Yellow''', '''Sixth White''', '''Seventh Red''', '''Eighth White''', and '''Ninth Purple'''.

The term "Nine Stars" can refer to several systems, and the one described here is specifically referred to as the "Purple White Nine Stars" or "Seven Colored Stars."

== Origin ==
The Nine Stars system originates from the following {{ill|magic square|ja|魔方陣|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/magic square|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/magic square|qq=}}:

== Nine Stars Comparison Chart ==
