According to legend, [[:en:Yu the Great|Yu the Great]], founder of the {{ill|Xia Dynasty|ja|夏王朝|1=Xia dynasty|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 夏 (三代)}}, conceived this magic square when he encountered a sacred turtle emerging from the {{ill|Luo River|ja|洛水|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 洛河}}. This magic square is called the "Writing of the Luo" ({{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 河図洛書}}), one of the {{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|河図洛書|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}.

== The Nine Stars ==
In Japanese [[:en:Onmyōdō|Onmyōdō]], the following table associates the Nine Stars with the [[:en:Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|five elements]], [[:en:Cardinal direction|Five directions]], [[:en:Bagua|eight trigrams]], and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 運}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|qq=}} of directions based on a person's birth year.

