-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/water|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/water|13=User:Immanuelle/Water (wuxing)|lt=Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/water|13=User:Immanuelle/Water (wuxing)|lt=Water (水)|comment=doing this to prevent wrong interwiki linking by bot|1=Water (wuxing)|2=uk|3=Вода (У-сін)|4=als|5=Wasser in dr chinesische Fümf-Elemänt-Leer|6=bcl|7=Tubig (wuxing)|8=vi|9=Thủy (Ngũ hành)|10=pt|11=Água (astrologia)|lt=Water (水)|qq=}}), the {{ill|Heavenly Stems|en|Heavenly Stems|WD=Q1190985|lt=ten heavenly stems|1=Heavenly Stems}}, the {{ill|Earthly Branches|en|Earthly Branches|WD=Q1072961|lt=twelve earthly branches|1=Earthly Branches}}, and the {{ill|Bagua|en|Bagua|WD=Q340846|lt=eight trigrams|1=Bagua}} of {{ill|I Ching|en|I Ching|WD=Q181937|lt=I Ching|1=I Ching}}. When these numbers shift positions, interpretations are added to form the "Nine Stars."

According to legend, {{ill|Yu the Great|en|Yu the Great|WD=Q627784|lt=Yu the Great|1=Yu the Great}}, founder of the {{ill|Xia Dynasty|ja|夏王朝|1=Xia dynasty|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia Dynasty|13=User:Immanuelle/Xia dynasty|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 夏 (三代)|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q169705}}, conceived this magic square when he encountered a sacred turtle emerging from the {{ill|Luo River|ja|洛水|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Luo River|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 洛河|1=Luo River (Henan)|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q1204978}}. This magic square is called the "Writing of the Luo" ({{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|洛書|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 河図洛書}}), one of the {{ill|Hetu and Luoshu|ja|河図洛書|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hetu and Luoshu|qq=}}.

== The Nine Stars ==
In Japanese {{ill|Onmyōdō|en|Onmyōdō|WD=Q1340540|lt=Onmyōdō|1=Onmyōdō}}, the following table associates the Nine Stars with the {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|en|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|WD=Q218652|lt=five elements|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)}}, {{ill|Cardinal direction|en|Cardinal direction|WD=Q23718|lt=Five directions|1=Cardinal direction}}, {{ill|Bagua|en|Bagua|WD=Q340846|lt=eight trigrams|1=Bagua}}, and colors, forming the '''Nine Stars Chart''' used to predict {{ill|fortune|ja|運勢|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/fortune|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 運|1=Luck|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q1970348}} and the {{ill|auspiciousness|ja|吉凶|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/auspiciousness|1=Q11412675|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11412675}} of directions based on a person's birth year.

